                <pb facs="0220" n="210" xml:id="pg210"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">714.44A15/242: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Guatemala</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Des Portes</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-05-24T13:00:00-06:00">May 24, 1941—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 3:54 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>71. My telegram no. 70, May 23, 1 p.m. The Chief of Protocol has just called at
                    the Legation with a message from President Ubico in which the President confirms
                    the Foreign Minister’s statement.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Des Portes</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
